course: dictionary
lesson: 3837
title: Two weeks, one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A fortnight is a word for a period of time. It means two weeks, or fourteen days. «A fortnight is two weeks, so it is 14 days.» You can check any new time word by counting the days in it.
explain: Look at the words around fortnight to see how it is used. «Sam is teased for a fortnight» means the teasing lasted two weeks. «She listens, writes it all down, and within a fortnight he moves to a new family» means the move happens inside two weeks.
explain: Fortnight is mostly used in Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand. People in the USA and Canada usually say two weeks instead. Both mean the same thing, so you can understand either one.
fact: A fortnight means two weeks, which is fourteen days.
fact: Phrases with fortnight: a fortnight ago (two weeks back), in a fortnight (two weeks from now), every fortnight (every two weeks).
fact: Fortnightly means happening every two weeks.
fact: To work out a number of fortnights, multiply by 14: 2 fortnights is 2 × 14 = 28 days.
fact: Fortnight is mainly used in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand; the USA and Canada usually say two weeks.
exercise: «A fortnight is two weeks, so it is 14 days.» How many days are in a fortnight? | 21 | 28 | *14 | 7
exercise: Sam is teased «for a fortnight». How long did the teasing last? | One day | *Two weeks | One month | Three days
exercise: Mum says, «We go to the beach in a fortnight.» When will they go? | Yesterday | Right now | Tomorrow | *Two weeks from now
test: «2 fortnights and 3 days» is how many days in total? | 17 | *31 | 42 | 28
test: Which word means happening every two weeks? | Yearly | Weekly | *Fortnightly | Daily
exam: «For a fortnight the teacher did not notice, until the book fell apart in her hands.» How long did the teacher not notice? | Two days | *Fourteen days | A whole month | One afternoon
